			<item>
				<title>About Me</title>
				<link>https://zzzyc001.github.io/about.html</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 26 Aug 2024 20:00:00 +0800</pubDate>
				<guid>https://zzzyc001.github.io/about.html</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;lede&#34; id=&#34;hello-im-yuechen-zhu&#34;&gt;Hello, I&#39;m Yuechen Zhu&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure class=&#34;right&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://zzzyc001.github.io/img/live_image_crop.jpg&#34;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;alt=&#34;Live Figure&#34; width=&#34;1000&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I got my Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science and Technology, Turing Class, Peking University. During my undergraduate years, I work closely with &lt;a href=&#34;https://binwangbfa.github.io/&#34;&gt;Dr. Bin Wang&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://baoquanchen.info/&#34;&gt;Prof. Baoquan Chen&lt;/a&gt;. I am seeking for PhD opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My research interests lie in physical simulations, Discrete Differential Geometry (DDG), and Computer Graphics (CG) in general. I would like to apply fields like differential geometry, differential equations, and computational mathematics to offer more intuitive and profound insights into our understanding of the world. The integration of diverse disciplines promises to endow us with a more comprehensive perspective toward&#xA;the world.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
